## Model card (rumored specifications — none verified)

- **Name:** Grok 5 (xAI next flagship; unreleased)
- **Short description:** xAI's next-generation flagship, reportedly in active training on Colossus 2 (xAI's ~2GW supercluster, ~520K GB200 + 30K GB300 GPUs). Every published release window (late 2025, Q1 2026, Q2 2026) has passed without a release; full API access was "expected Q3 2026" as of the most recent tracker (2026-07-08).
- **Provider / access:** xAI — not yet available. xAI's official model & pricing documentation (2026-09-21) lists grok-4.6 / 4.5 / 4.3 / 4.20 / build-0.1 and no grok-5; no announcement exists on x.ai/news.
- **Release / knowledge:** Unreleased as of 2026-10-03 (latest evidence: still training, 2026-07-08).
- **IDs:** `opencode/grok-5` (repo meta.json, stale stub: "128K total", "Text in/out", "Standard pricing").
- **Context window:** Rumored 1.5–2M tokens (unconfirmed; confidence "medium" at best per trackers).
- **Modalities:** Rumored native text/image/audio/video (unconfirmed).
- **Pricing:** Not announced; estimates ~$3–5 input / $15–20 output per 1M (unconfirmed).
- **Architecture:** Rumored ~6T-parameter MoE (a ~10T variant also rumored, less well-sourced); MoE means only a fraction of parameters activate per query.

## Raw benchmarks found

No verified public benchmark exists for Grok 5. One unverified leak ("Project Valis" candidate, reportedly 45.1% on a "Zeitgeist reasoning exam" vs Gemini 3 Pro's 32.4%) is flagged as unreliable — possibly cherry-picked or fabricated — and is not evidence.

For reference only (predecessor, verified): Grok 4 (2025-07) GPQA 87.0–87.5% / HLE 24.5% no-tools; Grok 4.20 (2026-03) GPQA 82.7% / HLE 22.8–30.0%.

## Normalized scores (1–100)

Not scored — the model is unreleased; any score would be fabricated from rumors. The repo's `average.md` (80.0, fallback mean of 1 source, no rater clears the >84.9 gate) cannot be reconciled with any public evidence located.

